Let $x$ be the number of guests.  The first venue costs $200 + 5x$ dollars, while the second venue costs $25x$ dollars.  We want to find the value of $x$ for which the two venues cost the same amount.  We can set up the equation $200 + 5x = 25x$ and solve for $x$:
\begin{align*}
200 + 5x &= 25x \\
200 &= 25x - 5x \\
200 &= 20x \\
x &= \frac{200}{20} \\
x &= \boxed{10}
\end{align*}
The answer is: 10

